The project is set up with Gravity UI. I need to implement a button that opens a modal with text and two actions — confirm and cancel. Gravity UI has `Modal` and `Button` components. There's also a `Dialog` component which is designed exactly for this — a dialog with confirm/cancel actions.

Gravity UI's Dialog component: `<Dialog open={open} onClose={...}>` with `Dialog.Header`, `Dialog.Body`, `Dialog.Footer` (which takes props like `onClickButtonCancel`, `onClickButtonApply`, `textButtonCancel`, `textButtonApply`).

Since the request is in Russian, I'll make the UI text in Russian: "Подтвердить" and "Отмена".

Let me write the App.tsx:

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { Button, Dialog, Modal } from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

export function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);

  const handleConfirm = () => {
    setOpen(false);
  };

  const handleCancel = () => {
    setOpen(false);
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ padding: 24 }}>
      <Button view="action" size="l" onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>
        Открыть окно
      </Button>
      <Dialog open={open} onClose={handleCancel} aria-labelledby="confirm-dialog-title">
        <Dialog.Header caption="Подтверждение" id="confirm-dialog-title" />
        <Dialog.Body>
          Вы уверены, что хотите выполнить это действие? Его нельзя будет отменить.
        </Dialog.Body>
        <Dialog.Footer
          onClickButtonApply={handleConfirm}
          onClickButtonCancel={handleCancel}
          textButtonApply="Подтвердить"
          textButtonCancel="Отмена"
        />
      </Dialog>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Wait — Dialog.Header caption prop. In Gravity UI, Dialog.Header takes `caption` prop. Let me check the API for Dialog in @gravity-ui/uikit v7:

```tsx
<Dialog onClose={...} open={...}>
  <Dialog.Header caption="Title" />
  <Dialog.Body>Content</Dialog.Body>
  <Dialog.Footer
    onClickButtonCancel={...}
    onClickButtonApply={...}
    textButtonCancel="Cancel"
    textButtonApply="Apply"
    loading={...}
  />
</Dialog>
```

Yes, that's correct. Dialog.Footer also has `propsButtonApply` for setting view e.g. `view: 'action'` (default is action I believe... actually default apply button view is 'action'... Let me recall: Dialog.Footer default propsButtonApply view is "action"). Actually the default text for apply is "Done" and cancel is "Cancel" (localized via i18n). Setting textButtonApply/textButtonCancel explicitly is good.

Also good to add a visible result of the confirm action — maybe show an alert or state message. Simple approach: on confirm, could show a toast via Gravity UI's Toaster or just set some state text. To keep it simple but demonstrate the action, I can display a small text under the button like "Подтверждено ✓" after confirming. That makes the demo more complete. But keep it simple. I'll add a status message.

Also, using `<Dialog>` requires Modal internally — Dialog includes Modal. Fine.

One consideration: with React.StrictMode and Gravity UI Modal, everything works fine.

Also aria attributes: Dialog.Header caption accepts `id`? Actually Dialog.Header props: caption, insertBefore, insertAfter. There's no id prop I think... Let me not overcomplicate. Dialog has aria-labelledby support? Modal supports aria-* props passed through. To be safe, I'll keep it simple without aria props, or use caption only.

